WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.750
Being cast on Game of Thrones can be a mixed
blessing.

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:08.170
On one hand, acting in HBO's hottest series
can seriously boost your acting résumé.

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:12.549
On the other hand, given the show's history,
you're probably going to get killed off sooner

00:00:12.549 --> 00:00:15.580
or later — as this long list of casualties
can attest.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:19.570
Here's a look at some of the major characters
who have died on the show, and where the actors

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:21.400
who played them are today.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.650
Harry Lloyd - Viserys Targaryen

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:29.091
He was supposed to be the true King of Westeros,
but Viserys Targaryen was the first main character

00:00:29.091 --> 00:00:33.670
to meet his maker on Game of Thrones, when
Khal Drogo "crowned" him with molten gold

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:35.190
during season one.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:39.570
Actor Harry Lloyd has kept himself busy since
dying on Game of Thrones, continuing to act

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:42.620
on television and in movies like The Theory
of Everything.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:48.910
His next project is a starring role in the
2018 Starz sci-fi thriller series Counterpart.

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:51.280
Mark Addy - Robert Baratheon

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:55.960
After a hunting trip gone wrong in season
one, King Robert Baratheon, first of his name,

00:00:55.960 --> 00:01:00.589
died, prompting his best friend Ned Stark
to take action against the machinations of

00:01:00.589 --> 00:01:01.969
Cersei and Joffrey.

00:01:01.969 --> 00:01:06.690
Since leaving Thrones, star Mark Addy has
surfaced on several television series, including

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:09.360
Great Expectations and The Syndicate.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:15.360
More recently, Addy appeared in the 2016 miniseries
Jericho, and as a detective in the 2016 crime

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:17.370
drama series New Blood.

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:19.680
Sean Bean - Ned Stark

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:24.040
After Robert's death, Ned Stark tried to take
control, sending a letter to Robert's brother,

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:27.570
Stannis, inviting him to come take his rightful
place on the throne.

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:32.400
Unfortunately for Ned, Cersei was two steps
ahead of him, and Ned famously lost his head

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:35.140
on the executioner's block at the end of season
one.

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:39.660
"You know which is a sacrifice of himself
for his family, which is a very moving and

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:40.820
touching moment.

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:43.210
And a good way to go, really."

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:47.290
Although Bean has a reputation for being killed
off in many of his projects, he hasn't let

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:48.990
that stop his acting career.

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:53.900
Since Thrones, he's appeared in a variety
of projects, including The Martian and Legends,

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:58.750
and some of his other recent work includes
roles in the six-part BBC miniseries Broken

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:01.560
and the 2017 thriller film Drone.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:03.610
Jason Momoa - Khal Drogo

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:07.860
Although Khal Drogo was dead essentially from
the moment that old evil witch lady infected

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:12.790
his wound with her fake medicine, his actual
death was much more tragic, as Daenerys had

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:16.700
to suffocate him with a pillow to put him
out of his misery at the end of season one.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:21.120
Jason Momoa's brief Game of Thrones tenure
served him well in Hollywood, leading to win

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:26.670
the role of Aquaman in the DC Extended Universe
films Batman v Superman, Justice League, and

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:29.450
2018's Aquaman solo adventure.

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:33.080
And Momoa seems like he's enjoying the ride.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:34.260
"Yahoo!"

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:40.200
Gethin Anthony - Renly Baratheon

00:02:40.209 --> 00:02:44.359
Following King Robert's death, his younger
brother Renly attempted to claim the throne.

00:02:44.359 --> 00:02:48.829
Renly had one of the largest armies in the
Seven Kingdoms and was beloved by everyone.

00:02:48.829 --> 00:02:53.890
Everyone except his brother Stannis, however,
who used black magic to murder Renly in season

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:54.890
two.

00:02:54.890 --> 00:03:00.030
After Game of Thrones, actor Gethin Anthony
appeared in the 2014 film Copenhagen as well

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:04.420
as the popular series Call The Midwife, then
demonstrated his range by playing Charles

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:07.799
Manson in the NBC period crime drama Aquarius.

00:03:07.799 --> 00:03:12.019
He also provided the voice of Gil Brodie in
the video game Mass Effect: Andromeda.

00:03:12.019 --> 00:03:14.599
Oona Chaplin - Talisa Maegyr

00:03:14.599 --> 00:03:19.349
Standing in for the book character of Jeyne
Westerling, Talisa Maegyr married Robb Stark,

00:03:19.349 --> 00:03:20.680
the King in the North.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:25.109
Unfortunately, Robb was already engaged to
the granddaughter of Lord Walder Frey, who

00:03:25.109 --> 00:03:29.540
exacted his revenge by murdering Talisa at
the Red Wedding in season three.

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:34.569
After Game of Thrones, Oona Chaplin starred
in the 2014 miniseries The Crimson Field and

00:03:34.569 --> 00:03:39.379
an episode of the popular television show
Black Mirror, as well as the 2015 movie The

00:03:39.379 --> 00:03:40.510
Longest Ride.

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:45.159
Some of her latest projects include starring
roles in the 2017 Spanish comedy film As We

00:03:45.159 --> 00:03:48.459
Like It, and the British drama series Taboo.

00:03:48.459 --> 00:03:50.200
Richard Madden - Robb Stark

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:54.680
The King in the North, Robb Stark met his
end beside his beloved Talisa, taking a knife

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:56.870
to the heart from the traitorous Roose Bolton.

00:03:56.870 --> 00:04:00.779
It was a traumatic way for actor Richard Madden
to end his time on the show.

00:04:00.779 --> 00:04:03.400
"I managed to get on the plane, covered in
fake blood.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.730
I was kinda upset at the end of the whole
job.

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:09.459
I kinda looked like I murdered someone and
got on the flight."

00:04:09.459 --> 00:04:15.040
Following his exit from Game of Thrones in
2014, Madden appeared in the series Medici:

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:20.100
Masters of Florence and as the Prince in the
2015 live-action Disney adaptation of Cinderella.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:25.320
More recently, Madden can be seen in the 2017
Amazon original series Oasis.

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:27.380
Michelle Fairley - Catelyn Stark

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:31.600
Though Catelyn dedicated her life to protecting
her children, she died at the Red Wedding

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:33.590
believing she had failed them all.

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:37.980
Since her terrible death in season three,
actress Michelle Fairley has stayed busy with

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:43.041
projects including the television series Resurrection
and the movie In the Heart of the Sea, as

00:04:43.041 --> 00:04:46.200
well as the Starz miniseries The White Princess.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:48.320
Jack Gleeson - Joffrey Baratheon

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:53.250
Thankfully, the reign of psychopathic boy
king Joffrey Baratheon's came to an early

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:54.250
end.

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:58.710
Joffrey married the widowed Margaery Tyrell,
but his reputation as an evil jerk preceded

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:03.650
him, so her grandmother protected her by slipping
some fast-acting poison into his cup at the

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:04.650
reception.

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:09.270
Jack Gleeson retired from screen acting after
Game of Thrones, but he remains involved in

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:10.270
the arts.

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:14.730
He founded Collapsing Horse Theatre Company
in Ireland, which won an award for their puppet

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:19.940
show Bears in Space at the 2016 1st Irish
Theatre Festival in New York City.

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:21.070
Thanks for watching!

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:24.100
